# RISC0 API Standards

## Context
- Applied when working with RISC0 v1.2.1 zero-knowledge proof system
- Serves as the primary entry point for RISC0-related rules
- References other RISC0 rules for specific implementation details

## Requirements

### Core API Usage
- Follow version-specific patterns for RISC0 v1.2.1
- Use correct type imports and module organization (see rule 2002-risc0-types)
- Handle receipts and proofs properly (see rule 2003-risc0-receipts)
- Implement guest programs correctly (see rule 2004-risc0-guest)
- Emit required metrics (see rule 2005-risc0-metrics)

### Version Compatibility
- Use RISC0 v1.2.1 API patterns:
  - Receipt types: `Receipt`, `InnerReceipt::Composite`, `InnerReceipt::Succinct`
  - Proof handling: `ProofJson`, `Seal`, `ProofDigest`
  - Guest program interface changes from pre-1.2.1
  - Updated metrics and proof size tracking

### Related Rules
- 2002-risc0-types: Type imports and organization
- 2003-risc0-receipts: Receipt and proof handling
- 2004-risc0-guest: Guest program implementation
- 2005-risc0-metrics: Metrics and monitoring

